.TH GARNER 1 "" "garner" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
garner \- internal repository for packages and container images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B garner
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B garner
is an internal repository for packages and container images.
It serves signed apt and dnf repositories from uploaded packages and from
releases synced from GitHub, GitLab and Forgejo/Gitea.
With the
.B oci
section configured it is also a container registry at
.IR /v2/ ,
which
.B docker push
and
.B docker pull
use, and syncs images from other registries; see
.BR garner.yaml (5).
Images are removed with
.B remove
like packages, by name and, as
.BR \-\-version ,
their digest.
.PP
Local commands run on the host that holds the configuration and the
database.
API commands talk to a running server over HTTP and can run anywhere.
Flags may appear before or after positional arguments;
.B \-\-
ends flag parsing.
A flag the command does not take is a usage error;
.B \-h
after a command lists the flags it takes.
.SH LOCAL COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve \fR[\fB\-\-config \fIFILE\fR]
Run the server.
.B SIGHUP
reloads the configuration;
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
stop it.
Under systemd it reports readiness through
.B \%NOTIFY_SOCKET
and accepts listening sockets passed with
.BR \%LISTEN_FDS .
.TP
.B init \fR[\fB\-\-config \fIFILE\fR]
Create the storage directory, the database, a signing key when
.B signing.keys
is empty, and an admin token.
The token is printed once.
Running it again keeps an existing key, and creates no token when any
token exists.
.TP
.BR "config validate" " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Check a configuration file and print its hash.
Works offline and does not open files that
.B *_file
keys point to.
.TP
.B token create \-\-name \fIN\fB \-\-owner \fIO\fB \-\-scope \fIS\fR[,\fIS\fR...]
.TQ
.B token list
.TQ
.B token revoke \fINAME\fR
Manage API tokens.
Scopes are
.BR upload ,
.B publish
and
.BR admin .
By default these open the database directly, which fails while
.B garner serve
runs; with
.B \-\-url
they go through the API and need an
.B admin
token.
.SH API COMMANDS
The server is taken from
.BR \-\-url ,
then
.BR GARNER_URL ,
then
.BR \%http://localhost:8080 .
Commands that change state need a token in
.B \%GARNER_TOKEN
with the scope listed.
Listing commands accept
.B \-\-json
to print the raw response.
.TP
.B upload \fR[\fB\-\-suite \fIS\fR] [\fB\-\-release \fIR\fR] \fIFILES\fR...
Upload .deb or .rpm files into a deb suite or rpm release.
Without them, packages go to the default one:
.B stable
if configured, else the first listed.
Scope:
.BR upload .
.TP
.B remove \fINAME\fR \fR[\fB\-\-version \fIV\fR] [\fB\-\-arch \fIA\fR] [\fB\-\-distribution \fID\fR]
Remove the matching versions of a package.
Scope:
.BR admin .
.TP
.B owner list
.TQ
.B owner set \fINAME OWNER\fR
Show or change which owner may upload a package name.
.B set
needs scope
.BR admin .
.TP
.B sync \fISOURCE\fR [\fB\-\-ignore\-age\fR \fITAG\fR [\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIREPO\fR]]
Start a sync of a configured source; follow it with
.BR "garner status" .
Scope:
.BR publish .
.IP
.B \-\-ignore\-age
lets the release
.I TAG
skip the source's
.BR min_release_age ,
for an urgent fix.
It covers only a release and package assets uploaded before the command
runs, so a release re-created under the same tag, or an asset uploaded
later, waits again; run it once the assets are attached.
.B \-\-repo
names the repository; it is required for
.B org
and
.B group
sources and must be one the source's last sync listed.
A tag that was already processed is refused, unless a release re-created
under it is waiting, and so is a source without
.BR min_release_age .
The decision is logged and kept with the token's name.
Needs scopes
.B publish
and
.BR admin .
.TP
.B approve \fIPACKAGE_ID\fR
Release a held package.
Fails when another file of the same version is already in the
distribution.
Scope:
.BR publish ;
a package held because its deliverer does not own the name needs
.B admin
as well.
.TP
.BR "conflicts list" " [" \-\-all ]
Show open conflicts, or all with
.BR \-\-all .
Only ownership conflicts are open, until the held package is approved or
removed; sync conflicts, such as a checksum mismatch, are listed with
.B \-\-all
only.
Scope:
.BR publish .
.TP
.B packages list \fR[\fB\-\-name \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-distribution \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR]
List packages; removed ones only with
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.B snapshot list
.TQ
.B snapshot rollback \fIID\fR
List published snapshots, or publish a new snapshot with the packages of
.IR ID .
.B rollback
needs scope
.BR publish .
.TP
.B publish
Publish a new snapshot.
Scope:
.BR publish .
.TP
.B gc
Delete package files and snapshots that are no longer referenced.
Scope:
.BR admin .
.TP
.B reload
Reload the server's configuration, like
.BR SIGHUP .
Scope:
.BR admin .
.TP
.B status
Show the version, configuration, current snapshot, open conflicts, held
packages and the state of each source.
.TP
.B verify \fR[\fB\-\-wait \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-hash \fIH\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR]
Check that the published repository is consistent and matches the
database, reading it as apt and dnf do: signatures against the published
keys, every index file by size and hash, each package in the indexes
against its pool file, and the index files of the previous snapshot.
Changes nothing; while it runs, publishes and GC wait.
Prints each problem as an
.B error
(a client can fail) or a
.B warning
(state the next publish or GC repairs, such as unreferenced files).
Scope:
.BR publish .
.IP
.B \-\-wait
retries for up to
.I D
(such as
.BR 5m )
while a publish is pending, so the check covers the latest uploads and
configuration.
.B \-\-config\-hash
also waits until the configuration whose sha256 starts with
.I H
(at least 7 hex digits) is loaded and published; without
.B \-\-wait
it waits up to 5 minutes.
Use it after pushing a configuration:
.BR "sha256sum garner.yaml" .
.B \-\-strict
exits 1 on warnings too.
.SH OTHER COMMANDS
.TP
.BR version ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GARNER_URL
Server URL for API commands and
.BR "token \-\-url" .
.TP
.B \%GARNER_TOKEN
API token as
.IB NAME : SECRET\fR,
as printed by
.B garner init
and
.BR "garner token create" .
It is sent only over https or to a loopback address.
.TP
.B GARNER_INSECURE_AUTH
Set to
.B 1
to send the token over plain http to any address, for isolated lab
networks; the server must allow it with
.BR server.allow_insecure_auth .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/garner/garner.yaml
Default configuration file; see
.BR garner.yaml (5).
.TP
.I /var/lib/garner
Default storage directory and SQLite database.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, at least one file of an upload failed, or
.B verify
found an error (with
.BR \-\-strict ,
also a warning).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
First start of a packaged install:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo -u garner garner init
systemctl enable \-\-now garner
.fi
.RE
.PP
Upload a package from CI:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export GARNER_URL=https://pkg.example.com
export GARNER_TOKEN=ci:...
garner upload \-\-suite stable dist/*.deb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check the repository after pushing a configuration change:
.PP
.RS
.nf
garner verify \-\-config\-hash "$(sha256sum garner.yaml | cut \-c1\-12)"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR garner.yaml (5),
.BR apt (8),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
